§ `If I do not move in -- the residence requirement`

-- Moved in after 3 months and lived there 14 months: met.
#ASSERT `Have I met the residence requirement` FALSE FALSE TRUE 3 14 12 12 EQUALS TRUE
-- Moved in after 13 months: not met.
#ASSERT `Have I met the residence requirement` FALSE FALSE TRUE 13 14 12 12 EQUALS FALSE
-- Moved in after 13 months with 18 months approved (s 76(1)): met.
#ASSERT `Have I met the residence requirement` FALSE FALSE TRUE 13 14 18 12 EQUALS TRUE
-- Moved in after 12 months exactly: 'within 12 months', met.
#ASSERT `Have I met the residence requirement` FALSE FALSE TRUE 12 14 12 12 EQUALS TRUE
-- Lived there 10 months: not met.
#ASSERT `Have I met the residence requirement` FALSE FALSE TRUE 3 10 12 12 EQUALS FALSE
-- Lived there 10 months with a shorter period of 9 approved (s 76(2)(a)): met.
#ASSERT `Have I met the residence requirement` FALSE FALSE TRUE 3 10 12 9 EQUALS TRUE
-- Never moved in: not met.
#ASSERT `Have I met the residence requirement` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 12 12 EQUALS FALSE
-- Never moved in, Permanent Forces and enrolled (s 76(6)): the requirement does not apply.
#ASSERT `Have I met the residence requirement` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 0 12 12 EQUALS TRUE
-- Never moved in, exempted by the Chief Commissioner (s 76(2)(b)).
#ASSERT `Have I met the residence requirement` FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 0 12 12 EQUALS TRUE
-- Approved in advance and never moved in: must notify and pay (s 76A(2)).
#ASSERT `Must I give notice and pay the relevant duty` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 12 12 EQUALS TRUE
-- Not approved in advance: s 76A(2) does not bind.
#ASSERT `Must I give notice and pay the relevant duty` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 12 12 EQUALS FALSE
-- Approved in advance and met.
#ASSERT `Must I give notice and pay the relevant duty` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 3 14 12 12 EQUALS FALSE
-- Completion 15 May 2025; the period allowed ends 15 May 2026 (READING, see NOTES.md); 14 days after: 29 May 2026.
#ASSERT `By what day must I give notice and pay the relevant duty` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 5 2025) 12 EQUALS (DATE_FROM_DMY 29 5 2026)
-- With 18 months approved: ends 15 November 2026; 14 days after: 29 November 2026.
#ASSERT `By what day must I give notice and pay the relevant duty` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 5 2025) 18 EQUALS (DATE_FROM_DMY 29 11 2026)
-- Completion 31 August 2025, 12 months: 31 August 2026 + 14 = 14 September 2026.
#ASSERT `By what day must I give notice and pay the relevant duty` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2025) 12 EQUALS (DATE_FROM_DMY 14 9 2026)
-- s 76A(3): the duty had the purchase not been eligible ($28,622 under H on $750,000) less any duty paid.
#ASSERT `How much relevant duty must I pay` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) 750000 750000 `one house or one flat` FALSE FALSE 16000 34000 91000 341000 1138000 3414000 0 EQUALS `the duty is` 28622
#ASSERT `How much relevant duty must I pay` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) 750000 750000 `one house or one flat` FALSE FALSE 16000 34000 91000 341000 1138000 3414000 1000 EQUALS `the duty is` 27622
#ASSERT `How much relevant duty must I pay` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) 750000 750000 `one house or one flat` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `not covered` `the amounts given for the year cannot be amounts adjusted under s 33AC`

§ `Transferring the home to my spouse`

-- Married, joint tenants after, their home, used only as a home, only the two of them: exempt (s 104B(1)).
#ASSERT `Is the transfer to my spouse exempt` `one house or one flat` `a married couple` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- De facto partners of 2 years or more: exempt.
#ASSERT `Is the transfer to my spouse exempt` `one house or one flat` `de facto partners who have lived in the relationship for at least 2 years` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- De facto partners of less than 2 years: not exempt (s 104B(1)(e)).
#ASSERT `Is the transfer to my spouse exempt` `one house or one flat` `de facto partners for less than 2 years` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Not a couple.
#ASSERT `Is the transfer to my spouse exempt` `one house or one flat` `not a couple` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- A house and a shop is s 104A residential land.
#ASSERT `Is the transfer to my spouse exempt` `one house or one flat, and a shop` `a married couple` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Vacant land they intend to build their home on.
#ASSERT `Is the transfer to my spouse exempt` `vacant land zoned for residential use` `a married couple` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Two or more dwellings is not s 104A residential land.
#ASSERT `Is the transfer to my spouse exempt` `two or more dwellings` `a married couple` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Unequal shares afterwards (s 104B(1)(a)).
#ASSERT `Is the transfer to my spouse exempt` `one house or one flat` `a married couple` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Not their principal place of residence (s 104B(1)(b)).
#ASSERT `Is the transfer to my spouse exempt` `one house or one flat` `a married couple` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Also used for other purposes (s 104B(1)(c)): not exempt, though s 104C may apply.
#ASSERT `Is the transfer to my spouse exempt` `one house or one flat` `a married couple` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Someone else is a party (s 104B(1)(d)).
#ASSERT `Is the transfer to my spouse exempt` `one house or one flat` `a married couple` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Exempt: nil.
#ASSERT `What transfer duty is payable on the transfer to my spouse` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2020) 0 400000 `one house or one flat` `a married couple` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `the duty is` 0
-- De facto of less than 2 years, a half share worth $400,000, 2019-20: $9,112 + $4.50 x 960 = $13,432.
#ASSERT `What transfer duty is payable on the transfer to my spouse` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2020) 0 400000 `one house or one flat` `de facto partners for less than 2 years` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `the duty is` 13432
-- The same under H, 1 March 2025: $10,217 + $4.50 x 590 = $12,872.
#ASSERT `What transfer duty is payable on the transfer to my spouse` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) 0 400000 `one house or one flat` `de facto partners for less than 2 years` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 FALSE 16000 34000 91000 341000 1138000 3414000 EQUALS `the duty is` 12872
-- s 104C, factor 0.2: duty on $400,000 x 0.2 = $80,000, range 3: $415 + $1.75 x 500 = $1,290.
#ASSERT `What transfer duty is payable on the transfer to my spouse` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2020) 0 400000 `one house or one flat` `a married couple` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 0.2 FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `the duty is` 1290
-- s 104C, factor 0.25: $100,000, range 4: $1,307 + $3.50 x 190 = $1,972.
#ASSERT `What transfer duty is payable on the transfer to my spouse` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2020) 0 400000 `one house or one flat` `a married couple` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 0.25 FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `the duty is` 1972
-- s 104C(6) shuts out s 32A: factor 0.9 on $4,000,000 = $3,600,000 at the general rate, $41,017 + $5.50 x 25,870 = $183,302.
#ASSERT `What transfer duty is payable on the transfer to my spouse` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2020) 0 4000000 `one house or one flat` `a married couple` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 0.9 FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `the duty is` 183302
-- Not a couple, $3,500,000 home: the premium rate, $184,702.
#ASSERT `What transfer duty is payable on the transfer to my spouse` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2020) 3500000 3500000 `one house or one flat` `not a couple` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `the duty is` 184702
-- Not a couple, $3,500,000, also used for other purposes: s 32B, not covered.
#ASSERT `What transfer duty is payable on the transfer to my spouse` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2020) 3500000 3500000 `one house or one flat` `not a couple` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 0 FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `not covered` `s 32B applies: residential land above the premium threshold used for other purposes; its apportionment factor is not encoded`
-- Before 1 July 2019, not exempt: not covered.
#ASSERT `What transfer duty is payable on the transfer to my spouse` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2019) 0 400000 `one house or one flat` `de facto partners for less than 2 years` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `not covered` `the liability arose before 1 July 2019, before the s 32 table in the deposit applied`
-- Before 1 July 2019 but exempt: nil, whatever the table.
#ASSERT `What transfer duty is payable on the transfer to my spouse` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2019) 0 400000 `one house or one flat` `a married couple` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `the duty is` 0

§ `Foreign persons -- surcharge purchaser duty`

-- A foreign person buying alone, $1,200,000: 9% = $108,000 (s 104U(1)).
#ASSERT `Do I owe surcharge purchaser duty, and how much` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) 1200000 1200000 `one house or one flat` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 0 FALSE EQUALS `the duty is` 108000
-- Foreign, as joint tenants with a citizen: 50% each (s 104V, s 14), $54,000 (s 104U(2)).
#ASSERT `Do I owe surcharge purchaser duty, and how much` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) 1200000 1200000 `one house or one flat` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 50 50 TRUE EQUALS `the duty is` 54000
-- Foreign, 25% as tenant in common with a citizen holding 75%: $27,000.
#ASSERT `Do I owe surcharge purchaser duty, and how much` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) 1200000 1200000 `one house or one flat` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 25 75 FALSE EQUALS `the duty is` 27000
-- A citizen buying with a foreign person: I owe none (s 104R(2)).
#ASSERT `Do I owe surcharge purchaser duty, and how much` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) 1200000 1200000 `one house or one flat` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 50 50 TRUE EQUALS `the duty is` 0
-- Both foreign, joint tenants: the whole $108,000.
#ASSERT `Do I owe surcharge purchaser duty, and how much` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) 1200000 1200000 `one house or one flat` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 50 50 TRUE EQUALS `the duty is` 108000
-- Price $1,000,000, worth $1,100,000: 9% of $1,100,000 = $99,000.
#ASSERT `Do I owe surcharge purchaser duty, and how much` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) 1000000 1100000 `one house or one flat` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 0 FALSE EQUALS `the duty is` 99000
-- Vacant residential land, $500,000: $45,000.
#ASSERT `Do I owe surcharge purchaser duty, and how much` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) 500000 500000 `vacant land zoned for residential use` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 0 FALSE EQUALS `the duty is` 45000
-- Two or more dwellings are residential land for Chapter 2A (s 104I(a)): $2,000,000 at 9% = $180,000.
#ASSERT `Do I owe surcharge purchaser duty, and how much` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) 2000000 2000000 `two or more dwellings` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 0 FALSE EQUALS `the duty is` 180000
-- Other land is not residential-related property.
#ASSERT `Do I owe surcharge purchaser duty, and how much` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) 1200000 1200000 `other land` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 0 FALSE EQUALS `the duty is` 0
-- Land used for primary production is not residential land (s 104I).
#ASSERT `Do I owe surcharge purchaser duty, and how much` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) 1200000 1200000 `one house or one flat` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 0 FALSE EQUALS `the duty is` 0
-- A foreign person holding a permanent visa: s 104ZKA may exempt; not encoded.
#ASSERT `Do I owe surcharge purchaser duty, and how much` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) 1200000 1200000 `one house or one flat` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 0 FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `a foreign transferee may be an exempt permanent resident or retirement visa holder (s 104ZKA, s 104ZKB); not encoded`
-- A foreign co-buyer holding a retirement visa: not encoded.
#ASSERT `Do I owe surcharge purchaser duty, and how much` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) 1200000 1200000 `one house or one flat` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 50 50 TRUE EQUALS `not covered` `a foreign transferee may be an exempt permanent resident or retirement visa holder (s 104ZKA, s 104ZKB); not encoded`
-- Also used for other purposes: s 104ZB, not encoded.
#ASSERT `Do I owe surcharge purchaser duty, and how much` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) 1200000 1200000 `one house or one flat` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 0 FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `the land is used for other purposes and the s 104ZB apportionment factor is not encoded`
-- Signed 31 December 2024: before the deposit's version date.
#ASSERT `Do I owe surcharge purchaser duty, and how much` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2024) 1200000 1200000 `one house or one flat` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 0 FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `the surcharge liability arose before 1 January 2025, the version date of the deposit; the commencement of the 9% rate is not in the deposit`
-- A foreign spouse taking a half share worth $500,000 from a citizen spouse owes $45,000: s 104ZK(2) keeps Part 8 (s 104B) away from surcharge purchaser duty.
#ASSERT `Do I owe surcharge purchaser duty, and how much` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) 0 500000 `one house or one flat` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 0 FALSE EQUALS `the duty is` 45000
-- The same transfer is exempt from transfer duty under s 104B.
#ASSERT `Is the transfer to my spouse exempt` `one house or one flat` `a married couple` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- s 104W: within 3 months after liability arises.
#ASSERT `By what day must I pay surcharge purchaser duty` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) EQUALS (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2025)

§ `Registering a car -- motor vehicle registration duty`

-- s 261: charged on a first registration, or a registration in a different name.
#ASSERT `Is my application charged with duty` FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my application charged with duty` TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my application charged with duty` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- s 266: the greater of price and market value, less GST on a Subdivision 38-P car and an extended warranty premium.
#ASSERT `What is the dutiable value of the vehicle` 55000 58000 0 0 EQUALS 58000
#ASSERT `What is the dutiable value of the vehicle` 55000 50000 5000 0 EQUALS 50000
#ASSERT `What is the dutiable value of the vehicle` 47000 40000 0 2000 EQUALS 45000

-- No exemption.
#ASSERT `Am I exempt from registration duty` FALSE FALSE `none, or less than 70% of the general rate` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Entitled on the registered owner's death (s 267(1)).
#ASSERT `Am I exempt from registration duty` TRUE FALSE `none, or less than 70% of the general rate` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- A relationship breakdown transfer (s 267(6)-(7)).
#ASSERT `Am I exempt from registration duty` FALSE TRUE `none, or less than 70% of the general rate` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- A veteran at 70% or more of the general rate (s 267(7A)(a)).
#ASSERT `Am I exempt from registration duty` FALSE FALSE `70% or more of the general rate (s 22(3))` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- A veteran on the special rate (s 267(7A)(d)).
#ASSERT `Am I exempt from registration duty` FALSE FALSE `the special rate (s 24)` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- MRCA, 50 impairment points and compensation received (s 267(7AA)).
#ASSERT `Am I exempt from registration duty` FALSE FALSE `none, or less than 70% of the general rate` 50 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- MRCA, 40 points: not enough.
#ASSERT `Am I exempt from registration duty` FALSE FALSE `none, or less than 70% of the general rate` 40 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- MRCA, 60 points but no compensation or pension.
#ASSERT `Am I exempt from registration duty` FALSE FALSE `none, or less than 70% of the general rate` 60 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Conditional registration (s 267(7B)).
#ASSERT `Am I exempt from registration duty` FALSE FALSE `none, or less than 70% of the general rate` 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Registered by me in another state with duty paid there (s 268).
#ASSERT `Am I exempt from registration duty` FALSE FALSE `none, or less than 70% of the general rate` 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- A new $30,000 car: $3 x 300 = $900 (s 265(1)).
#ASSERT `What duty do I pay to register this vehicle` FALSE FALSE `a vehicle constructed primarily to carry not more than 9 occupants` 30000 30000 0 0 FALSE FALSE `none, or less than 70% of the general rate` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 900
-- $30,050: a part of $100 counts, $3 x 301 = $903.
#ASSERT `What duty do I pay to register this vehicle` FALSE FALSE `a vehicle constructed primarily to carry not more than 9 occupants` 30050 30050 0 0 FALSE FALSE `none, or less than 70% of the general rate` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 903
-- A $45,000 car: a passenger vehicle, $1,350 + 0 = $1,350 (s 265(2)).
#ASSERT `What duty do I pay to register this vehicle` FALSE FALSE `a vehicle constructed primarily to carry not more than 9 occupants` 45000 45000 0 0 FALSE FALSE `none, or less than 70% of the general rate` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 1350
-- $45,000.50 passenger: $1,350 + $5 x 1 = $1,355.
#ASSERT `What duty do I pay to register this vehicle` FALSE FALSE `a vehicle constructed primarily to carry not more than 9 occupants` 45000.5 45000.5 0 0 FALSE FALSE `none, or less than 70% of the general rate` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 1355
-- $45,000.50 goods vehicle: $3 x 451 = $1,353.
#ASSERT `What duty do I pay to register this vehicle` FALSE FALSE `another vehicle` 45000.5 45000.5 0 0 FALSE FALSE `none, or less than 70% of the general rate` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 1353
-- A $60,000 car: $1,350 + $5 x 150 = $2,100.
#ASSERT `What duty do I pay to register this vehicle` FALSE FALSE `a vehicle constructed primarily to carry not more than 9 occupants` 60000 60000 0 0 FALSE FALSE `none, or less than 70% of the general rate` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 2100
-- A $60,000 motor cycle: $3 x 600 = $1,800.
#ASSERT `What duty do I pay to register this vehicle` FALSE FALSE `a motor cycle` 60000 60000 0 0 FALSE FALSE `none, or less than 70% of the general rate` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 1800
-- A $100,000 car: $1,350 + $5 x 550 = $4,100.
#ASSERT `What duty do I pay to register this vehicle` FALSE FALSE `a vehicle constructed primarily to carry not more than 9 occupants` 100000 100000 0 0 FALSE FALSE `none, or less than 70% of the general rate` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 4100
-- Price $55,000, market value $58,000: $1,350 + $5 x 130 = $2,000.
#ASSERT `What duty do I pay to register this vehicle` FALSE FALSE `a vehicle constructed primarily to carry not more than 9 occupants` 55000 58000 0 0 FALSE FALSE `none, or less than 70% of the general rate` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 2000
-- A Subdivision 38-P car, $55,000 including $5,000 GST: $50,000, $1,350 + $5 x 50 = $1,600.
#ASSERT `What duty do I pay to register this vehicle` FALSE FALSE `a vehicle constructed primarily to carry not more than 9 occupants` 55000 50000 5000 0 FALSE FALSE `none, or less than 70% of the general rate` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 1600
-- $47,000 including a $2,000 extended warranty premium: $45,000, $1,350.
#ASSERT `What duty do I pay to register this vehicle` FALSE FALSE `a vehicle constructed primarily to carry not more than 9 occupants` 47000 47000 0 2000 FALSE FALSE `none, or less than 70% of the general rate` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 1350
-- A used $25,000 car transferred to me: $3 x 250 = $750.
#ASSERT `What duty do I pay to register this vehicle` TRUE FALSE `a vehicle constructed primarily to carry not more than 9 occupants` 25000 25000 0 0 FALSE FALSE `none, or less than 70% of the general rate` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 750
-- Re-registered in the same name: not charged (s 261).
#ASSERT `What duty do I pay to register this vehicle` TRUE TRUE `a vehicle constructed primarily to carry not more than 9 occupants` 60000 60000 0 0 FALSE FALSE `none, or less than 70% of the general rate` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
-- Inherited (s 267(1)).
#ASSERT `What duty do I pay to register this vehicle` FALSE FALSE `a vehicle constructed primarily to carry not more than 9 occupants` 60000 60000 0 0 TRUE FALSE `none, or less than 70% of the general rate` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
-- A veteran at 70% or more of the general rate.
#ASSERT `What duty do I pay to register this vehicle` FALSE FALSE `a vehicle constructed primarily to carry not more than 9 occupants` 60000 60000 0 0 FALSE FALSE `70% or more of the general rate (s 22(3))` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
-- MRCA 50 points and compensation.
#ASSERT `What duty do I pay to register this vehicle` FALSE FALSE `a vehicle constructed primarily to carry not more than 9 occupants` 60000 60000 0 0 FALSE FALSE `none, or less than 70% of the general rate` 50 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
-- Registered interstate by me, duty paid there (s 268).
#ASSERT `What duty do I pay to register this vehicle` FALSE FALSE `a vehicle constructed primarily to carry not more than 9 occupants` 60000 60000 0 0 FALSE FALSE `none, or less than 70% of the general rate` 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS 0

-- s 262: a statement of dutiable value goes with every application chargeable with duty.
#ASSERT `Must I lodge a statement of the dutiable value` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `none, or less than 70% of the general rate` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I lodge a statement of the dutiable value` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `none, or less than 70% of the general rate` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
